    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d631">

                <pb facs="1061" n="965" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg965"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.529/26</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Spanish Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Amoedo</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-08-27"><hi rendition="#italic">August 27,
                        1926</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 67–19</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: Referring to previous notes of
                    this Embassy of His Majesty and to those from the State Department dealing with
                    the Convention between Spain and the United States concerning alcoholic
                    beverages and this Convention having been signed by the parties concerned and
                    ratified by the Senate of the United States<anchor n="15" xml:id="d631-f1"/> in
                    order that the Spanish vessels which may call at the ports of the United States
                    may have no trouble in the matter with the customs authorities and the
                    prohibition officers and in particular in the ports of New York, San Juan, Porto
                    Rico, Galveston, Texas, Houston, Texas, New Orleans, Louisiana, and Mobile,
                    Alabama, where vessels most often call, I beg your Excellency kindly to issue
                    appropriate instructions to the authorities at those ports in the sense that
                    effect may be given to the said Convention.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mariano Amoedo</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d631-f1" n="15" xml:id="d631-f1-content">
                <p>Ratification advised by the Senate, Mar. 3, 1926; ratified by the President, Mar.
                    30, 1926.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
